# This configuration file is set up the following way:
#
# The first field is the name of the binary, the second is the arguments in
# shell-quoted form, the third is padding, and the remainder are attributes.
# An attribute is `t` if the value must be true to select this editor, `n` if
# it must be false, and `a` if the editor will work in either case.
#
# The attributes are as follows:
#
# detach - This editor detaches from the terminal.
# console - This editor requires a console (command-line interface, not necessarily a TTY).
# dumb - This editor works in a dumb terminal.
# display - This editor requires a GUI.
# remote - This editor will work on a remote system (e.g., via SSH).
